rse the place was full  so i had to sit down with  other people  and there were two  ladies there and so i started up a  conversation and we had a great  conversation so there you go uh it is  possible on occasion to stripe up strike  up conversations with random people i  have had two lessons a day here an hour  in the morning and an hour half in the  afternoon  with the two of my tutors so that's kind  of my  guaranteed daily check  and then the  the first day that i was here which was  tuesday night the first full day uh we  had a  20 somehow more than 20 people showed up  for our meetup at the uh  novo mizki uh pivovar  and i have some video of that and uh if  i can figure out how to get it on to  youtube youtube i'm going to for some  reason the file seems very long but  we'll figure it out at any rate that was  solid check for a good four hours or so  so that first day was a lot of check uh  the second day a little bit less but i  had to run some errands and do some  things  but today i had my lesson this morning  i'm having lunch with one of the people  who  came and i must say all the people who  came to the dinner were  keeners on learning language people who  follow me here on youtube  many of them spoke several languages  one of them mikhail  said you know if you have time give me a  call we'll have lunch he's a lawyer here  in prague so we're going to have lunch  in a couple of hours  and then we're meeting again tonight  with zdeniak who has come up from bruno  with his girlfriend and yarda is going  to be with me again he was there of  course tuesday night and  there was another gentleman i think  ronald was his name who teaches four  different languages and he and possibly  another person are going to come so  we'll have another solid check evening  tonight  tomorrow i'm invited by gabriella and  jan to their home at night that'll be  some solid check uh plus uh we're having  lunch with zuzana and her husband are  gonna visit a museum uh we'll see how  much check we get in there so yeah i'm  getting enough opportunity but but the  bigger thing is that just  i think the biggest thing of all is like  how much i will improve i don't know  however the  sense of satisfaction from the minute i  got on the plane in london and they made  the public address system on the  airplane in check and i understood what  they were saying that's a wonderful  feeling uh to fly into a place and all  of a sudden you know what they're saying  everything around me i understand i can  read it i can read the signs  if i have to for example i got on the  tramway uh and the conductor said you  know you can't buy tickets here and i  said well where do i buy them he says i  don't know you get a lot of that here  you know where i don't know  okay so but then i go ask a few people  on the street and they spoke to me and  checked and directed me finally to a  place where i could buy the ticket for  the tramway a very handy weather  excellent system i should say again that  my morning my morning uh the classes are  the best because my hotel is right by  the charles  bridge  and the charles bridge is probably the  most international place in the world  you hear every possible language there  and it's just chock-a-block  with tourists but at seven in the  morning as i walk across the bridge it's  just spectacular the sun is rising  there's no one on the bridge i see all  of prague in front of me it's just it's  just wonderful and spectacular uh but i  was going to say the biggest advantage  of  if you remember my strategy  five days to fluency the whole idea is  that you plan for this  five days which hopefully for most  people is longer than five days but i  only have five days so you prepare for  this is my goal i have to be functional  when i get there in six months in a year  however long you give yourself  and so then i did a lot of listening and  reading built up my vocabulary with two  months to go i started  increasing you know the frequency of my  online discussions with my tutors so  when i get here i can function now i  wouldn't call myself fluent  uh although i'm going to put up some  videos of me speaking check but i'm  comfortable i understand what people  sing are saying to me i understand  conversations uh and that's a wonderful  feeling i think with that kind of a base  it doesn't take you long  to start using it even though of course  you stumble and make  all kinds of grammatical mistakes when  speaking the language  uh i think it it takes you to a new  level but i think the impact is not  immediate i don't think you come here  and in three days bingo you're fluent  but i think it what i feel about it is  that it it puts you in a different state  you've lived now in the language for  five days it's no longer something  that's artificial  you've been immersed to it in it  and i think you come away with that with  a lot of things that are going to  continue to grow with you a different  attitude to the language because you've  known you now know that you can actually  function in the language  um  and i think uh yeah  the effects will be felt over a longer  period of time the other thing you of  course notice is that having done a lot  of listening to radio and things about  history and stuff you're missing the  day-to-day um the day-to-day day-to-day  words  uh i met this american girl in the  bookstore  and  she had a lot of the day-to-day language  but she said that she was very afraid to  go to  the countryside where  people don't speak english because she's  afraid that she might be in a situation  where she just couldn't find her way  back or that there would be no one there  who would understand what she was saying  or that she wouldn't understand and i  don't have that fear at all because i  understand what people are saying so i  might have difficulty i might be missing  a few words very common words in fact  that i haven't come across  but i'm totally comfortable that i  understand what people are saying and i  could stumble my way through to explain  anything that i need to explain but  that's certainly not fluency anyway just  a short term uh here uh report and we'll  see we can load this video up and i  pardon i apologize for the lighting here  in my room thank you for listening and  bye for oh one very important thing all  those people who came to the dinner  uh and many of them expressed the desire  to get together again even when i'm not  here of course there's a little group of  keen language learners a group of  linkers and of course i tremendously  encourage that we didn't have all have a  chance to exchange emails if all the  people who are there or anybody else who  wants to be part  uh of a group whether in prague or  really anywhere send me your email at  steveatlinklingq.com  send me your email and i will find a way  to share these emails around everyone  that sends me an email so if you're at  the dinner or you want to belong to a  group of language cleaners or linkers  please send me your email at steve link  lingq dot com thank you bye

